{
 "lesson": 39,
 "duration": 743.5680625,
 "segments": [
  {
   "start": 0.34,
   "end": 3.34,
   "text": "What was to go in French?"
  },
  {
   "start": 3.34,
   "end": 5.34,
   "text": "Aller."
  },
  {
   "start": 5.34,
   "end": 9.34,
   "text": "And we are going, we go."
  },
  {
   "start": 9.34,
   "end": 11.34,
   "text": "Nous allons."
  },
  {
   "start": 11.34,
   "end": 14.34,
   "text": "We are going to eat."
  },
  {
   "start": 14.34,
   "end": 18.34,
   "text": "Nous allons manger."
  },
  {
   "start": 18.34,
   "end": 25.34,
   "text": "So, nous allons manger means both we are going to eat, like, you know, talking about the future, we're going to eat."
  },
  {
   "start": 25.34,
   "end": 30.34,
   "text": "And also, literally, we are going to eat, like, we are going somewhere to eat."
  },
  {
   "start": 30.34,
   "end": 34.34,
   "text": "What was I go, I'm going?"
  },
  {
   "start": 34.34,
   "end": 37.34,
   "text": "Je vais."
  },
  {
   "start": 37.34,
   "end": 46.34,
   "text": "So, Aller has many highly irregular forms now because they actually come from another verb that fused with Aller to make a set."
  },
  {
   "start": 46.34,
   "end": 49.34,
   "text": "The same has happened in English, actually, with to go."
  },
  {
   "start": 49.34,
   "end": 55.34,
   "text": "But in the past, the past form of to go in English, went, comes from a totally different verb."
  },
  {
   "start": 55.34,
   "end": 58.34,
   "text": "Went isn't from to go, no, but it is its past."
  },
  {
   "start": 58.34,
   "end": 65.34,
   "text": "So the idea of different verbs marrying into one verb, let's say, isn't too alien to us as English speakers."
  },
  {
   "start": 65.34,
   "end": 69.34,
   "text": "So we have to go, Aller, we go alone."
  },
  {
   "start": 69.34,
   "end": 73.34,
   "text": "But I go, I'm going, vais, the AIS, je vais."
  },
  {
   "start": 73.34,
   "end": 76.34,
   "text": "I'm going to eat."
  },
  {
   "start": 76.34,
   "end": 78.34,
   "text": "Je vais manger."
  },
  {
   "start": 78.34,
   "end": 80.34,
   "text": "Je vais manger."
  },
  {
   "start": 80.34,
   "end": 83.58,
   "text": "I want to eat."
  },
  {
   "start": 83.58,
   "end": 86.58,
   "text": "Je veux manger."
  },
  {
   "start": 86.58,
   "end": 91.58,
   "text": "So that's maybe a slight difference now to a new way to French, especially if people are speaking quickly."
  },
  {
   "start": 91.58,
   "end": 93.58,
   "text": "Je vais manger."
  },
  {
   "start": 93.58,
   "end": 94.58,
   "text": "I'm going to eat."
  },
  {
   "start": 94.58,
   "end": 96.58,
   "text": "Je veux manger."
  },
  {
   "start": 96.58,
   "end": 97.58,
   "text": "I want to eat."
  },
  {
   "start": 97.58,
   "end": 101.58,
   "text": "So we have je vais, I go, and you go, you're going."
  },
  {
   "start": 101.58,
   "end": 105.02,
   "text": "Tu vais."
  },
  {
   "start": 105.02,
   "end": 106.02,
   "text": "VS."
  },
  {
   "start": 106.02,
   "end": 108.02,
   "text": "Tu vas."
  },
  {
   "start": 108.02,
   "end": 112.02,
   "text": "He goes or she goes is il va or elle va."
  },
  {
   "start": 112.02,
   "end": 118.02,
   "text": "We have the same as in tu vas, but the va of il or elle is just VA, just VA."
  },
  {
   "start": 118.02,
   "end": 120.02,
   "text": "But of course that sounds the same as tu vas."
  },
  {
   "start": 120.02,
   "end": 122.02,
   "text": "What is he going to do?"
  },
  {
   "start": 122.02,
   "end": 125.02,
   "text": "Let's use qu'est-ce for what?"
  },
  {
   "start": 125.02,
   "end": 127.02,
   "text": "What is he going to do?"
  },
  {
   "start": 127.02,
   "end": 130.34,
   "text": "Qu'est-ce qu'est-ce qu'il?"
  },
  {
   "start": 130.34,
   "end": 131.34,
   "text": "Very good."
  },
  {
   "start": 131.34,
   "end": 133.34,
   "text": "Va faire?"
  },
  {
   "start": 133.34,
   "end": 134.34,
   "text": "Very good."
  },
  {
   "start": 134.34,
   "end": 135.34,
   "text": "Qu'est-ce qu'il va faire?"
  },
  {
   "start": 135.34,
   "end": 137.34,
   "text": "What is he going to do?"
  },
  {
   "start": 137.34,
   "end": 139.34,
   "text": "What is it that he is going to do?"
  },
  {
   "start": 139.34,
   "end": 144.34,
   "text": "And we have that contraction now between qu'est-ce qu'il va faire?"
  },
  {
   "start": 144.34,
   "end": 147.34,
   "text": "Isn't he going to do anything?"
  },
  {
   "start": 147.34,
   "end": 149.34,
   "text": "Isn't he going to do anything?"
  },
  {
   "start": 149.34,
   "end": 154.65,
   "text": "Il ne va pas faire rien."
  },
  {
   "start": 154.65,
   "end": 156.65,
   "text": "How was not anything?"
  },
  {
   "start": 156.65,
   "end": 158.65,
   "text": "Not nothing."
  },
  {
   "start": 158.65,
   "end": 159.65,
   "text": "How do we build that construction?"
  },
  {
   "start": 159.65,
   "end": 161.65,
   "text": "What do we use?"
  },
  {
   "start": 161.65,
   "end": 162.65,
   "text": "Neu prion."
  },
  {
   "start": 162.65,
   "end": 163.65,
   "text": "Neu prion."
  },
  {
   "start": 163.65,
   "end": 164.65,
   "text": "Good."
  },
  {
   "start": 164.65,
   "end": 165.65,
   "text": "So let's try that again."
  },
  {
   "start": 165.65,
   "end": 167.65,
   "text": "Isn't he going to do anything?"
  },
  {
   "start": 167.65,
   "end": 173.65,
   "text": "Il ne va faire rien."
  },
  {
   "start": 173.65,
   "end": 174.65,
   "text": "Good."
  },
  {
   "start": 174.65,
   "end": 176.65,
   "text": "Il ne va rien faire."
  },
  {
   "start": 176.65,
   "end": 177.65,
   "text": "No."
  },
  {
   "start": 177.65,
   "end": 178.65,
   "text": "So in French we say,"
  },
  {
   "start": 178.65,
   "end": 181.65,
   "text": "he isn't going anything to do."
  },
  {
   "start": 181.65,
   "end": 182.65,
   "text": "No."
  },
  {
   "start": 182.65,
   "end": 184.65,
   "text": "Because we have neu and rien,"
  },
  {
   "start": 184.65,
   "end": 186.65,
   "text": "which is our negation of anything."
  },
  {
   "start": 186.65,
   "end": 189.65,
   "text": "Il ne va rien faire."
  },
  {
   "start": 189.65,
   "end": 191.65,
   "text": "So I go, I'm going is je vais,"
  },
  {
   "start": 191.65,
   "end": 193.65,
   "text": "you go, you're going,"
  },
  {
   "start": 193.65,
   "end": 197.65,
   "text": "tu vas and he or she goes or is going,"
  },
  {
   "start": 197.65,
   "end": 199.65,
   "text": "il va, elle va."
  },
  {
   "start": 199.65,
   "end": 201.65,
   "text": "So we've seen how in French we can talk about the future"
  },
  {
   "start": 201.65,
   "end": 203.65,
   "text": "using the present tense."
  },
  {
   "start": 203.65,
   "end": 204.65,
   "text": "No."
  },
  {
   "start": 204.65,
   "end": 207.65,
   "text": "Either with the present of a verb and some future context"
  },
  {
   "start": 207.65,
   "end": 209.65,
   "text": "like je le fais demain."
  },
  {
   "start": 209.65,
   "end": 213.65,
   "text": "Ce soir, no, I'm doing it tomorrow or tonight."
  },
  {
   "start": 213.65,
   "end": 215.65,
   "text": "Or we can use the verb to go,"
  },
  {
   "start": 215.65,
   "end": 217.65,
   "text": "aller, to go into the future."
  },
  {
   "start": 217.65,
   "end": 222.65,
   "text": "We can also use the present to talk about the past in French."
  },
  {
   "start": 222.65,
   "end": 225.65,
   "text": "Again in much the same way as we do in English."
  },
  {
   "start": 225.65,
   "end": 227.65,
   "text": "What was the word for I in French?"
  },
  {
   "start": 227.65,
   "end": 228.65,
   "text": "I?"
  },
  {
   "start": 228.65,
   "end": 229.65,
   "text": "Je."
  },
  {
   "start": 229.65,
   "end": 230.65,
   "text": "Je."
  },
  {
   "start": 230.65,
   "end": 231.65,
   "text": "I have."
  },
  {
   "start": 231.65,
   "end": 233.65,
   "text": "I have in French is je."
  },
  {
   "start": 233.65,
   "end": 235.65,
   "text": "This is spelled J,"
  },
  {
   "start": 235.65,
   "end": 237.65,
   "text": "apostrophe A-I."
  },
  {
   "start": 237.65,
   "end": 239.65,
   "text": "So have there is A-I,"
  },
  {
   "start": 239.65,
   "end": 240.65,
   "text": "et,"
  },
  {
   "start": 240.65,
   "end": 241.65,
   "text": "but je"
  },
  {
   "start": 241.65,
   "end": 242.65,
   "text": "and"
  },
  {
   "start": 242.65,
   "end": 243.65,
   "text": "et"
  },
  {
   "start": 243.65,
   "end": 244.65,
   "text": "contract"
  },
  {
   "start": 244.65,
   "end": 245.65,
   "text": "and we get je."
  },
  {
   "start": 245.65,
   "end": 247.65,
   "text": "Je apostrophe A-I."
  },
  {
   "start": 247.65,
   "end": 248.65,
   "text": "Je."
  },
  {
   "start": 248.65,
   "end": 249.65,
   "text": "So that means I have,"
  },
  {
   "start": 249.65,
   "end": 251.65,
   "text": "how much you say I have it?"
  },
  {
   "start": 252.65,
   "end": 253.65,
   "text": "Je l'ai."
  },
  {
   "start": 253.65,
   "end": 254.65,
   "text": "Je l'ai."
  },
  {
   "start": 254.65,
   "end": 255.65,
   "text": "Very good."
  },
  {
   "start": 255.65,
   "end": 256.65,
   "text": "No, we have je"
  },
  {
   "start": 256.65,
   "end": 259.65,
   "text": "and then le and et will contract to give us le."
  },
  {
   "start": 259.65,
   "end": 260.65,
   "text": "Je l'ai."
  },
  {
   "start": 260.65,
   "end": 263.65,
   "text": "That's spelled L, apostrophe A-I."
  },
  {
   "start": 263.65,
   "end": 264.65,
   "text": "Very good."
  },
  {
   "start": 264.65,
   "end": 265.65,
   "text": "I have them."
  },
  {
   "start": 267.65,
   "end": 268.65,
   "text": "Je l'ai."
  },
  {
   "start": 268.65,
   "end": 269.65,
   "text": "Je l'ai."
  },
  {
   "start": 269.65,
   "end": 270.65,
   "text": "Je l'ai."
  },
  {
   "start": 270.65,
   "end": 271.65,
   "text": "Je l'ai."
  },
  {
   "start": 271.65,
   "end": 272.65,
   "text": "Very good."
  },
  {
   "start": 272.65,
   "end": 273.65,
   "text": "Je l'ai."
  },
  {
   "start": 273.65,
   "end": 275.65,
   "text": "So have here, no, it's just A-I, et."
  },
  {
   "start": 275.65,
   "end": 276.65,
   "text": "So in English,"
  },
  {
   "start": 276.65,
   "end": 278.65,
   "text": "most we have a past tense for example,"
  },
  {
   "start": 278.65,
   "end": 279.65,
   "text": "I ate."
  },
  {
   "start": 279.65,
   "end": 280.65,
   "text": "No."
  },
  {
   "start": 280.65,
   "end": 281.65,
   "text": "I ate."
  },
  {
   "start": 281.65,
   "end": 282.65,
   "text": "I ate."
  },
  {
   "start": 282.65,
   "end": 284.65,
   "text": "We can also just say I have eaten"
  },
  {
   "start": 284.65,
   "end": 286.65,
   "text": "and the same goes for French"
  },
  {
   "start": 286.65,
   "end": 288.65,
   "text": "and in French it's actually much more common to say"
  },
  {
   "start": 288.65,
   "end": 290.65,
   "text": "I have eaten than I ate."
  },
  {
   "start": 290.65,
   "end": 292.65,
   "text": "This is the most used past"
  },
  {
   "start": 292.65,
   "end": 294.65,
   "text": "in spoken French."
  },
  {
   "start": 294.65,
   "end": 297.65,
   "text": "So that's a very useful structure for us."
  },
  {
   "start": 297.65,
   "end": 299.65,
   "text": "So we would begin with I have,"
  },
  {
   "start": 299.65,
   "end": 300.65,
   "text": "je,"
  },
  {
   "start": 300.65,
   "end": 301.65,
   "text": "but we need to find"
  },
  {
   "start": 301.65,
   "end": 302.65,
   "text": "eaten"
  },
  {
   "start": 302.65,
   "end": 304.65,
   "text": "to say I have eaten,"
  },
  {
   "start": 304.65,
   "end": 306.65,
   "text": "which is a very easy form to find."
  },
  {
   "start": 306.65,
   "end": 308.65,
   "text": "For ER verbs,"
  },
  {
   "start": 308.65,
   "end": 310.65,
   "text": "we remove our ER ending"
  },
  {
   "start": 310.65,
   "end": 312.65,
   "text": "to get this form like eaten from manger"
  },
  {
   "start": 312.65,
   "end": 314.65,
   "text": "and we put an E"
  },
  {
   "start": 314.65,
   "end": 316.65,
   "text": "with an accent"
  },
  {
   "start": 316.65,
   "end": 318.65,
   "text": "to make us hear that E on the end"
  },
  {
   "start": 318.65,
   "end": 320.65,
   "text": "and we get manger."
  },
  {
   "start": 320.65,
   "end": 322.65,
   "text": "So it sounds the same as the two verbs"
  },
  {
   "start": 322.65,
   "end": 324.65,
   "text": "manger to eat"
  },
  {
   "start": 324.65,
   "end": 326.65,
   "text": "with the ER ending and then manger"
  },
  {
   "start": 326.65,
   "end": 328.65,
   "text": "with an E"
  },
  {
   "start": 328.65,
   "end": 330.65,
   "text": "with a written accent, meaning eaten"
  },
  {
   "start": 330.65,
   "end": 332.65,
   "text": "but sounding exactly like"
  },
  {
   "start": 332.65,
   "end": 334.65,
   "text": "to eat, manger."
  },
  {
   "start": 334.65,
   "end": 336.65,
   "text": "So I have eaten."
  },
  {
   "start": 336.65,
   "end": 338.65,
   "text": "Je mange"
  },
  {
   "start": 338.65,
   "end": 340.65,
   "text": "So this manger"
  },
  {
   "start": 340.65,
   "end": 342.65,
   "text": "is spelled M-A-N-G-E"
  },
  {
   "start": 342.65,
   "end": 344.65,
   "text": "and that E has the accent"
  },
  {
   "start": 344.65,
   "end": 346.65,
   "text": "on the top, the one that goes"
  },
  {
   "start": 346.65,
   "end": 348.65,
   "text": "down from right to left."
  },
  {
   "start": 348.65,
   "end": 350.65,
   "text": "Je mange. I have eaten."
  },
  {
   "start": 350.65,
   "end": 352.65,
   "text": "I haven't eaten."
  },
  {
   "start": 352.65,
   "end": 354.65,
   "text": "Je n'ai pas mangé."
  },
  {
   "start": 354.65,
   "end": 356.65,
   "text": "Je n'ai pas mangé."
  },
  {
   "start": 356.65,
   "end": 358.65,
   "text": "Very good. So ne"
  },
  {
   "start": 358.65,
   "end": 360.65,
   "text": "is ne and E"
  },
  {
   "start": 360.65,
   "end": 362.65,
   "text": "have contracting."
  },
  {
   "start": 362.65,
   "end": 364.65,
   "text": "Je n'ai"
  },
  {
   "start": 364.65,
   "end": 366.65,
   "text": "pas mangé."
  },
  {
   "start": 366.65,
   "end": 368.65,
   "text": "Je n'ai pas mangé."
  },
  {
   "start": 368.65,
   "end": 370.65,
   "text": "What was the word for again"
  },
  {
   "start": 370.65,
   "end": 372.65,
   "text": "like when we ask for another song?"
  },
  {
   "start": 372.65,
   "end": 374.65,
   "text": "encore"
  },
  {
   "start": 374.65,
   "end": 376.65,
   "text": "encore, good. pas encore"
  },
  {
   "start": 376.65,
   "end": 378.65,
   "text": "pas encore"
  },
  {
   "start": 378.65,
   "end": 380.65,
   "text": "Here we have an option of the very"
  },
  {
   "start": 380.65,
   "end": 382.65,
   "text": "common liaison. pas encore"
  },
  {
   "start": 382.65,
   "end": 384.65,
   "text": "we can use for not yet."
  },
  {
   "start": 384.65,
   "end": 386.65,
   "text": "Literally not again, pas encore"
  },
  {
   "start": 386.65,
   "end": 388.65,
   "text": "meaning not yet"
  },
  {
   "start": 388.65,
   "end": 390.65,
   "text": "and pas encore"
  },
  {
   "start": 390.65,
   "end": 392.65,
   "text": "combines with ne."
  },
  {
   "start": 392.65,
   "end": 394.65,
   "text": "If you wanted to say I haven't"
  },
  {
   "start": 394.65,
   "end": 396.65,
   "text": "eaten yet, how might that be?"
  },
  {
   "start": 396.65,
   "end": 398.65,
   "text": "I haven't eaten yet."
  },
  {
   "start": 398.65,
   "end": 400.65,
   "text": "I haven't yet eaten."
  },
  {
   "start": 400.65,
   "end": 402.65,
   "text": "Je n'ai pas encore mangé."
  },
  {
   "start": 402.65,
   "end": 404.65,
   "text": "Perfect. Je n'ai pas"
  },
  {
   "start": 404.65,
   "end": 406.65,
   "text": "encore mangé."
  },
  {
   "start": 406.65,
   "end": 408.65,
   "text": "Je n'ai pas"
  },
  {
   "start": 408.65,
   "end": 410.65,
   "text": "encore mangé."
  },
  {
   "start": 410.65,
   "end": 412.65,
   "text": "I have eaten it."
  },
  {
   "start": 412.65,
   "end": 414.65,
   "text": "How would you say that? I have"
  },
  {
   "start": 414.65,
   "end": 416.65,
   "text": "eaten it."
  },
  {
   "start": 416.65,
   "end": 418.65,
   "text": "Je l'ai mangé."
  },
  {
   "start": 418.65,
   "end": 420.65,
   "text": "I have eaten them."
  },
  {
   "start": 420.65,
   "end": 422.65,
